course: dictionary
lesson: 5625
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it to find the right one. This is its context. «Lily found it under a desk and gave it back to him without reading a word.» Here Lily is a girl's name, because someone found something and gave it back.
explain: «Lily» can also name a flower. A lily grows from a bulb and has large trumpet-shaped flowers. «Frogs sit on lily pads» tells you it means a water lily, a plant with round leaves that float on a pond. Ask: does the sentence describe a person or a plant?
explain: Some phrases change the meaning completely. «He is not lily-white in this matter» does not mean he is a flower. It means he is not completely innocent. When you meet a word in a phrase, read the whole phrase and check that your meaning still makes sense.
fact: A lily is a flowering plant that grows from a bulb, with large trumpet-shaped flowers, often white, orange or pink.
fact: A water lily is a plant with round leaves that float on ponds.
fact: Lily is also a common girl's first name, as in «Lily invited girls from both streets to her birthday».
fact: «Lily-white» means very white, or completely innocent.
fact: Lilies are very poisonous to cats, even the pollen, so keep them away from cats.
exercise: «Lily invited girls from both streets to her birthday, and her mum had to buy twice as many party bags.» In this sentence, what is Lily? | A water lily on a pond | *A girl's name, a person who has a birthday | A plant with trumpet flowers | A lily-white shade of paint
exercise: «Frogs sit on lily pads.» What is a lily pad? | A lily-white bag | A bulb that grows in the ground | A flower petal | *A round leaf that floats on a pond
exercise: «He is not lily-white in this matter.» What does lily-white mean here? | Very white in colour | Ready for a funeral | *Completely innocent, not blameless | Very tall
test: «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» Who is Lily in this sentence? | A lily-white cloth | A flower with petals | A lily pad on a pond | *A girl's name
test: In science, why are lilies used for labelled flower diagrams? | They are used to make bulbs | They are grown only in gardens | *They have clear parts: petals, stamens with pollen, and a pistil | They float on water
exam: Why must a pet cat be kept away from lilies? | Lilies are soft and cats hurt themselves | Lilies stop cats from sleeping | Cats like to sit on lily pads | *Lilies are very poisonous to cats, even the pollen
